{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsq8RGKestsLocY72Z7C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`, but I could not run it end to end. On this Mac it refuses to start until `CODEX_API_KEY` is set. The codex login here is a ChatGPT login in `~/.codex/auth.json`, and the sandbox has to block that file.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`run.sh`**: the new lane runs the same `codex exec` command as the `codex` lane, wrapped in `sandbox-exec -f sandbox/agent.sb`. `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME` point at an empty scratch dir that is removed afterwards.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`**: the profile used to re-open `~/.kimi-code` for every lane. I checked that a shell under the profile could list that directory, so reusing the profile unchanged would have left part of the real home readable to the codex lane. The re-opened path is now a parameter, `OPEN`. Kimi passes `~/.kimi-code` as before. Codex passes its scratch dir and opens nothing under the real home.\n- **`README.md`**: documents the lane and the `OPEN` parameter.\n- **`ANSWER.md`**: the write-up you asked for, including what I did not verify.\n\n**Verification (local only)**\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n- Running the lane without `CODEX_API_KEY` exits 2 with a clear message.\n- Under the profile, a shell in the codex lane cannot read `~/.codex/auth.json`, list `~/.codex`, or write to `~/.codex`. It also cannot read `~/.kimi-code`.\n- The kimi lane still lists its own `~/.kimi-code/bin`.\n- `codex` starts under the profile with a scratch `CODEX_HOME` and no sandbox errors.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I did not run a real task through `codex exec`, because that sends the prompt to OpenAI. I also have not confirmed that `codex exec` accepts `CODEX_API_KEY` on this CLI version.\n- The sandboxed codex lane does not load `~/.codex/config.toml`, so its MCP servers and plugins are absent. The config sets no model, so both lanes use the default model.\n\n**Decision for you:** the lane needs a credential it can use without the real home. I used `CODEX_API_KEY`, which the README already describes. I did not copy `auth.json` into the scratch dir, because that would hand the shell the login itself. If you would rather use the ChatGPT login, that is a design change and needs your call.\n\nNothing was committed, deployed, published or sent to an external service. I left `/tmp/chome-UT8cZY` alone; it predates this session and is not from my tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":46043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b8b5e51-0646-4c86-b37e-ab3744a76fda","uuid":"480c5638-2fa4-4976-bae4-32f092005c3b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:30:48.206Z","request_id":"req_011Cgsq8R6QXncrM9ySp43h4"}
